# 95_hui_electrocuted_x4 — FIVE held-HP electrocute attempts in one run
# (14z-96). The consumer question is the maintainer's 2026-08-18 grunt
# report: on merged-m2, Phobos has an extra grunt after the electrocution
# EVERY OTHER time (their capture: 4 electrocutions, grunts after #2 and
# #4). A period-2 phenomenon needs >= 4 events in ONE run to show its
# period; replay 93 produces exactly one clean electrocute, so this exists.
#
# Same skeleton as 93_hui_electrocuted (same forced-pick pokes: P1=0x10
# Phobos victim, P2=0x03 Victor attacker — 0x03 is Victor on vsav AND
# vsav2, one script serves both legs). Setup and FIRST attempt are
# byte-identical to replay 93 (walk-in 2900-3200, approach 3250-3370,
# held HP 3400-3470). Then a ~650-frame cycle: re-approach walk (~120f,
# Phobos gets pushed back by the hit) + the next 70-frame held HP.
#
# ATTEMPT WINDOWS (for consumers): 3400, 4050, 4700, 5350, 6000. Five
# attempts so that one whiff still leaves the four a period-2 readout
# needs. Every attempt is the HELD version — replay 93's section-2 lesson
# stands: a short press is the QUICK version and does NOT electrocute, so
# a consumer must assert class 0x07 + freeze >= 0x2f PER ATTEMPT before
# reading anything from its tail (an attempt that merely hit, or whiffed,
# is not an electrocution and its tail proves nothing about the grunt).
#
# P2 stands on the RIGHT, so his forward is LEFT (`L`); button 3 is HP.
